osxaudio: stop the AudioUnit when the ring buffer pauses

A paused HAL output unit kept running and fed silence, so Core Audio's IO
thread woke the process about 90 times a second for as long as the sink was
paused. The ring buffer pauses under its object lock with its waiters
released, exactly as it stops, so the render callback cannot be waiting on
that lock, and AudioOutputUnitStop is as safe here as in the stop path.

--- a/sys/osxaudio/gstosxcoreaudiohal.c	2026-09-07 15:11:13.000000000 -0400
+++ b/sys/osxaudio/gstosxcoreaudiohal.c	2026-11-09 17:18:12.000000000 -0500
@@ -1007,15 +1007,10 @@
     GST_DEBUG_OBJECT (core_audio,
         "osx ring buffer pause ioproc: %p device_id %lu",
         core_audio->element->io_proc, (gulong) core_audio->device_id);
-    if (core_audio->io_proc_active) {
-      /* CoreAudio isn't threadsafe enough to remove the render callback in the
-       * render notify callback, so we pause by having the callback drop
-       * samples or feed silence. See:
-       * http://lists.apple.com/archives/Coreaudio-api/2006/Mar/msg00010.html
-       * https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/issues/4155
-       */
-      g_atomic_int_set (&core_audio->io_proc_dropping, TRUE);
-    }
+    /* The ring buffer pauses from a streaming or state-change thread under its
+     * object lock, with its waiters released, as it stops; the AudioUnit stops
+     * as it does on stop, and its render callback is removed once it has. */
+    gst_core_audio_io_proc_stop (core_audio);
   }
   return TRUE;
 }
